[38;5;252m[1m## What the project turned out to be[0m[0m
[0m[0m
A single-function library: [38;5;10mvoid colourblind(cb_impairment, float *R, float *G, float *B)[0m applies one of three 3×3 dichromacy matrices in place. [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m declares [1mno [38;5;10m[features][0m[22m and [38;5;10mCMakeLists.txt[0m has [1mno build options[22m, so there is exactly one configuration to verify. I still swept it in both the [38;5;10mdev[0m and [38;5;10mrelease[0m profiles, since those hand LLVM different optimisation levels — and that turned out to matter.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## The one real bug found[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation was numerically correct for all finite and infinite inputs but produced different [1mNaN payloads[22m than C.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
On x86, [38;5;10mADDSS[0m/[38;5;10mSUBSS[0m return the [3mdestination[23m (left) operand when it is NaN, falling back to the source only otherwise. Which product term the compiler puts on the left is a codegen choice, and GCC at [38;5;10m-O0[0m and LLVM at [38;5;10m-O3[0m disagree — LLVM additionally rewrites [38;5;10msum - c*B[0m into [38;5;10m(-c)*B + sum[0m, flipping the winner. I read the intended operand order off the C disassembly for all nine channel expressions and encoded it in the data flow via [38;5;10maddss[0m/[38;5;10msubss[0m helpers.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two follow-on traps along the way:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- A static "first NaN input wins" precedence table is wrong. With [38;5;10mR = G = +inf[0m, the intermediate [38;5;10m+inf + -inf[0m raises invalid-operation and produces the default QNaN [38;5;10m0xffc00000[0m [3mmid-chain[23m, which then outranks a NaN that arrived as an input.[0m[0m
- LLVM folds [38;5;10misnan(a + b)[0m into [38;5;10misnan(a) || isnan(b)[0m — unsound for exactly that case — and collapsed my helpers back into the wrong table. [38;5;10mcore::hint::black_box[0m on the helper results is what forces the intermediate to actually be tested.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Testing[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mtranslation/tests/ffi_parity.rs[0m — 12 tests, all [38;5;10mdlopen[0ming both libraries and calling [38;5;10mcolourblind[0m purely through its exported symbol, comparing [38;5;10mto_bits()[0m rather than [38;5;10mf32[0m equality so [38;5;10m±0.0[0m and NaN payloads are not conflated. Coverage: unit-range grid, exhaustive cross products of edge/special/overflow values, a full 254-exponent sweep, ~1.2M random bit patterns, aliased pointers (the C helpers copy all three inputs before storing, so aliasing has observable semantics), out-of-range impairments (the C [38;5;10mswitch[0m has no [38;5;10mdefault:[0m, so the triple must be untouched), and 1000-iteration feedback loops.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mverify.sh[0m enumerates the feature powerset, builds the C reference, then per combination and profile runs [38;5;10mcargo check --all-targets[0m, [38;5;10mcargo build[0m, [38;5;10mcargo test[0m, and diffs [38;5;10mnm -D[0m. [38;5;10mcolourblind[0m is the only symbol the C [38;5;10m.so[0m defines (the rest of its [38;5;10mnm -D[0m output is weak [3mundefined[23m imports) and the Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m exports it.[0m[0m
